Upstream fix for sst/opencode (verified against b731bc1).

`core/src/filesystem.ts` and `core/src/filesystem/search.ts` import each other.
As ESM source the cycle is benign. Published through `Bun.build({ splitting:
true })` both modules land in ONE chunk with `filesystem.ts` emitted first, so
its top-level `deps: [..., FileSystemSearch.node]` reads the search namespace
before that module has run and captures `undefined`. Every request whose layer
tree reaches `@opencode/FileSystem` then dies in `LayerNode.walk` with
`TypeError: undefined is not an object (evaluating 'node.name')`, which the
router returns as an empty 500.

`search.ts` only needs `FindInput` and `Entry`, both of which come from
`@opencode-ai/schema/filesystem`. Importing them from there instead of from
`../filesystem.js` breaks the cycle, and the bundler then emits the two modules
in separate chunks with a real import edge between them.

Verified in the upstream repo at b731bc1:
  before: packages/core built dist -> config.get/agent.list/provider.list/plugin.list all ERR
  after : the same four calls all OK, matching source behaviour.

